      "title": "Program Specialist | Criminology & Criminal Justice Department (Pullman, WA)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOnline applications must be received before 11:59pm on: September 30, 2026 If a date is not listed above, review the Applicant Instructions below for more details. Available Title(s): 107I-YN_CS_NPS - Program Specialist 2 Business Title: Program Specialist | Criminology & Criminal Justice Department (Pullman, WA) Employee Type: Classified Position Details: The Opportunity: The Criminal Justice and Criminology Department at Washington State University is seeking a Program Specialist to support the Washington State Data Exchange for Public Safety (WADEPS) . As the Program Specialist, you will assist with administrative, help desk, and fiscal support for the WADEPS project. The primary function of your role is to provide a wide range of administrative and operational support in a fast-paced and high-volume environment. Your duties include, but are not limited to help desk and project coordination, aiding in personnel and payroll processes, staff/faculty recruitment, office activities and events, purchasing, accounts payable, travel, and financial activities for   WADEPS , as well as providing similar support for reporting units as needed. When necessary, you will represent the Executive Director at meetings involving internal and external institutional partners and maintain the Executive Director's calendar. You   will serve as the primary organizational point of contact for the Executive Director and   WADEPS   staff to support organizational partnering, manage correspondence, and refer inquiries to the appropriate offices using independent judgment, discretion, and follow-ups. Additional Information: This is a full-time (100% FTE), permanent position. This position is overtime-eligible . Monthly Salary: $3,827 to $5,111 | Range 42 | Steps A-M | Successful candidates are typically hired at the beginning of the salary range and receive scheduled salary increment increases in accordanc